        "original_id": "e9928434-a13f-56bc-8332-a17aac26f78f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Manettia, Fragaria\n- People: Saverio Manetti, Giovanni Targioni Tozzetti, Carolus Linnaeus\n- Organizations: Orto Botanico di Firenze\n- Places: Florence\n- Concepts: plant taxonomy, flowering plants, genus naming\n\nFacts:\n- Giovanni Targioni Tozzetti was supervisor of the Orto Botanico di Firenze in Florence before Saverio Manetti succeeded him.\n- Carolus Linnaeus named the plant genus Manettia in honor of Saverio Manetti.\n- Manettia is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rubiaceae.\n- Fragaria is a genus of flowering plants in the family Rosaceae.\n- Fragaria plants are commonly known as strawberries because of their edible fruits.",
